	<a class="btn btn-primary" href="/signup/">Free trial</a>
	<a class="btn btn-secondary" href="{{ site.voicemlReferenceUrl }}/nouns/conference/">&lt;Conference&gt; reference</a>
</p>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>What callers get</h2>
	<ul class="features-grid">
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "headset" %}</span>
			<h3>A moderator</h3>
			<p>Calls from the control room&rsquo;s numbers open the bridge, and the bridge closes when they hang up.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "clock" %}</span>
			<h3>Hold until it starts</h3>
			<p>Staff and visitors who call before the control room hear hold music, not silence.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "telephone" %}</span>
			<h3>Staff who speak</h3>
			<p>Pressing 1 joins the bridge with a voice.</p>
		</li>
		<li class="feature">
			<span class="feature-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% icon "broadcast-pin" %}</span>
			<h3>Visitors who listen</h3>
			<p>Pressing 2 joins muted, without the join tone, to hear the bridge without interrupting it.</p>
		</li>
	</ul>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Before you start</h2>
	<ol>
		<li><strong>A VoiceML account with a phone number.</strong> See <a href="/voiceml/">VoiceML</a> or <a href="/signup/">start a free trial</a>.</li>
		<li><strong>The numbers the control room calls from</strong>, in E.164 format.</li>
	</ol>
	<div class="alert alert-warning" role="note">
		<p><strong>The control room numbers in this document are fictional.</strong> They use the 555-0100 to 555-0199 range, which is set aside for fiction. Replace them with your own before you publish.</p>
	</div>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Step 1: Publish the document and point the number at it</h2>
	<p>Replace the control room numbers with your own, then publish it at <a href="{{ site.voicemlPublisherUrl }}">voiceml.org</a> and set the <code>/r/</code> URL it returns as the phone number&rsquo;s voice URL. Keep the URL exactly as returned, <code>key</code> included, and don&rsquo;t post it publicly.</p>
	<p class="code-block-header">main.xml</p>
	<pre class="code-block" data-lang="xml"><code>{{ voicemlSamples["park-incident-bridge"].main | escape }}</code></pre>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>Step 2: Test it</h2>
	<ol>
		<li>From a phone that isn&rsquo;t on the control room list, call and press 1. You hear hold music.</li>
		<li>From a control room phone, call the same number. The bridge opens and the two calls are connected.</li>
		<li>From a third phone, call and press 2. You hear the other two, but they can&rsquo;t hear you.</li>
		<li>Hang up the control room phone. The other two calls leave the bridge and hear that it has closed.</li>
	</ol>
</section>

<section class="section-block">
	<h2>How the bridge works</h2>
	<p>Everyone joins the same room with <code>&lt;Dial&gt;&lt;Conference&gt;isla-nublar-incident&lt;/Conference&gt;&lt;/Dial&gt;</code>. Room names are private to your account, so another account using the same name gets a separate room. What differs between callers is the attributes:</p>
	<div class="table-container">
		<table class="data-table">
			<caption>The &lt;Conference&gt; attributes for each kind of caller</caption>
			<thead>
				<tr>
					<th scope="col">Attribute</th>
					<th scope="col">Control room</th>
					<th scope="col">Staff</th>
					<th scope="col">Visitors</th>
				</tr>
			</thead>
			<tbody>
				<tr><td><code>startConferenceOnEnter</code></td><td><code>true</code>: starts the bridge</td><td><code>false</code>: waits on hold</td><td><code>false</code>: waits on hold</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>endConferenceOnExit</code></td><td><code>true</code>: closes it for everyone</td><td>Default <code>false</code></td><td>Default <code>false</code></td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>muted</code></td><td>Default <code>false</code></td><td>Default <code>false</code></td><td><code>true</code>: heard by no one</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>beep</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td><code>true</code></td><td><code>false</code>: joins without a tone</td></tr>
				<tr><td><code>participantLabel</code></td><td><code>control-room</code></td><td><code>staff</code></td><td><code>visitor</code></td></tr>
			</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<p>None of them sets <code>waitUrl</code>, so callers waiting for the control room hear the platform&rsquo;s default hold playlist. The control room is recognized by <code>From</code>, using the same Liquid list check as the <a href="/support/voiceml/build-call-screening-with-voiceml/">call screening example</a>; everyone else chooses with a key. When a participant leaves the room, the document carries on after the <code>&lt;Dial&gt;</code>, which is where staff and visitors hear that the bridge has closed.</p>
</section>

